# Canonical organization names (DevLog-006). Key = canonical org_name, value = names used in affiliation batches.
# Rule: one name per organization (its own short English name/brand); legal suffixes and word-order variants merge;
# distinct legal entities, spin-offs and renamed organizations stay separate (printed name kept):
#   Xperi vs Adeia (spin-off 2022), Showa Denko Materials vs Resonac (renamed 2023),
#   Tokyo Institute of Technology vs Institute of Science Tokyo (merged 2024), ASE vs SPIL (separate subsidiaries).
TSMC: [Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company, TSMC]
ASE: [Advanced Semiconductor Engineering, "Advanced Semiconductor Engineering, Inc.", ASE Group]
A*STAR: [A*STAR, "Agency for Science, Technology and Research"]
A*STAR Institute of Microelectronics: [A*STAR Institute of Microelectronics, "Institute of Microelectronics, A*STAR"]
Applied Materials: [Applied Materials, "Applied Materials, Inc."]
Dai Nippon Printing: [Dai Nippon Printing, "Dai Nippon Printing Co., Ltd."]
Deca Technologies: [Deca Technologies, Deca Technologies Inc.]
Fraunhofer IZM: [Fraunhofer IZM, Fraunhofer Institute for Reliability and Microintegration IZM]
Murata Manufacturing: [Murata Manufacturing, "Murata Manufacturing Co., Ltd."]
nepes: [Nepes, nepes Corporation]
nepes hayyim: [nepes hayyim, nepes hayyim Corporation]
Samsung Electronics: [Samsung Electronics, "Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd."]
SK hynix: [SK hynix, SK hynix Inc.]
SPIL: ["Siliconware Precision Industries Co., Ltd."]
Intel: [Intel Corporation]
